Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ledger: repair the register's own integrity (E30, E31);
 reconcile the v3.4 checksums; fix the index

The register is this project's only credential, so defects in it matter more
than defects anywhere else. The consistency audit found four.

- E31 (new): E8 had been assigned to TWO unrelated entries -- the 20 Aug
  strict-liability correction and the 19 Aug Sacramento-scorecard correction.
  The strict-liability entry keeps E8 because E12 cites it by number in
  published text; the scorecard entry is renumbered E30, carrying a note of
  its original number so old citations still land. Nothing deleted. A
  sequence check joins the push routine, since E14 had already repaired this
  exact failure mode for E13 and did not catch this instance.
- changelog: a dated checksum note on the v3.4 block. Two of the four
  published sha256 digests no longer reproduce -- NOT the statute or jacket,
  which still verify exactly, but the companion and regulations, both modified
  after tagging by the repo-wide dollar-escape pass and later edits. Current
  digests published beside the as-tagged ones; the as-tagged values are not
  amended, because a checksum in a changelog is a dated record. Same
  convention audit/record.md already uses for its chunk heads.
- LEDGER.md: the opening paragraph still said the three parts are 'merged
  here' and that 'new entries are written in the register you are reading
  now' -- untrue since the 21 Aug split, and contradicted eight lines later by
  'this file is now an index'. Rewritten as index prose; the duplicated
  part-i anchor removed (duplicate ids make the anchor's resolution
  undefined, and ledger/README promises it lands).
- errata: anchors added for E12, E14, E16, E25-E31 so the register's internal
  cross-references resolve; E24's three-doors link repointed from ./README.md
  (which is ledger/README.md) to ../README.md.
- diary: the Recent index gains 21 August, previously absent though it is the
  largest day in the record, and today's conformance pass.

Tagged v3.4 text unchanged (E10).
